    "source": "Emergent Mind daily digest emails (matt@emergentmind.com) of 2026-10-16, 2026-10-19 and 2026-10-20, 5 papers each, 15 total, added at the user's word (\"Add Oct 16-20 + run Grandmaster's Methods at recon\"). Every arXiv ID below was verified at the arXiv API by title search on 2026-10-20 (title, first author and published date match the email on all 15); the email itself carries no arXiv IDs (its links are Emergent Mind paper pages), so no ID is taken from the email. Grandmaster's Methods pass (Stunspot 2025-08-16, standing harvest pairing, docs/harvest-loop.md at b169e15) applied at recon, summary in the recon note: two author methods dominate the fragile end of this batch. (1) Validation-then-compression of the OpenAI October 2026 proof drops: Binder et al. validate the OpenAI Brennan/Kraetzer preprints and report a drastically shorter proof of a stronger statement; Banks re-arranges the OpenAI Landau-Siegel argument as a direct proof with explicit constants; Kerr simplifies the same OpenAI proof. The load-bearing question for all three is the same: does the compression preserve the source argument (M2), and does the simplified statement still say what the headline says (M1)? (2) LLM-as-proposer with a programmatic evaluator (quantum circuits, DiscoveryRSI, the Minecraft agents): the evaluator / task harness is the trusted base, and the headline inherits its fidelity (M4). Skeptic filters run: success-myth reconstruction is the live risk in secondary coverage of the Minecraft run (n=1, Easy difficulty, privileged symbolic state, 605 deaths, all disclosed in the paper's own framing as carried by the digest summary); ghosted-authorship and survivorship do not apply beyond the disclosed-LLM notes recorded per claim. One overlap: frei-sofos-widmer-quasi-riemann was announced in the 2026-10-16 email but was already queued 2026-10-18 and its audit CLOSED 2026-10-20 (main@ef465a7, V-A PARTIAL / V-B PARTIAL, Lean build GAP); it is listed for provenance only and is not a new pick."
